A||||21||mrfiero||I think I killed a Fiero!||||9||
Z||000000||mrfiero||11-17-2000||04:06 AM||||Well, I'm not sure yet, but I will find out later today.  Here's what happened......a guy calls me up saying his '87 SE 4cyl. is making a weird noise (I have done work on this Fiero before).  I drove to Denver to take a look. It sounded like it was coming from the valve train, so I removed the valve cover.  Everything looked OK so I reinstalled everything and thought about it and realized that it was coming from the alternator (I felt so stupid!).  I changed it out and all was well.  <P>I didn't use a new valve cover gasket (we were short on time and it was about 20* outside), but I didn't notice any leaks. I told him to keep an eye on things and if he noticed any oil leaking to give me a call.<P>At about 10 pm I get a call from him saying his Fiero was gone......it caught fire!!  I was floored.  He said it started sputtering then died.  He noticed smoke pouring from the trunk and opened it up to see flames shooting out.  By the time the fire truck arrived the rear was engulfed.....it's obviously totalled.  <P>I'm reserving any judgment until I can see it in person, but it's possible that the valve cover started leaking (badly) and either caught fire or drained it of enough oil to throw a rod through the block which started the fire.  Again, I'll know more later today.<P>How depressing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000001||2xsess||11-17-2000||07:09 AM||||Hopefully it's not your fault. But it's a sad sorry no matter what the cause. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>Jeff<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000002||ChadMan||11-17-2000||08:37 AM||||(moment of silence)||||reg||9
Z||000003||fldevel||11-17-2000||11:44 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> bummer ..****  happens though ||||reg||9
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||11-17-2000||12:14 PM||||It would take a LOT of oil to leak out to throw a rod. If thats what happened its more his fault than yours. If a person doesnt realize that all the oil is leaking (with the extream smell and smoke)... he/she shouldnt be driving a car.<P>Your off the hook  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>My 2 1/2 cents  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||7
Z||000005||StuGood||11-17-2000||01:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B> it was about 20* outside), but I didn't notice any leaks. I told him to keep an eye on things and if he noticed any oil leaking to give me a call.(</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, I'd say you're off the hook, alright.  Besides, from what  I've heard, sometimes it's tough to keep those 4-cylinders' valve covers from leaking even with a <B>new</B> gasket.  It's a shame, but these things happen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   Don't beat yourself up.||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||11-17-2000||03:35 PM||||My car is leaking antifreeze and oil...can't figure out where the leak is for sure!!! <BR>This is very bad, and of course, its a L4.<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 11-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||11-17-2000||05:20 PM||||My dad's 87 Fiero has been leaking significant amounts of oil from the valve cover for a few years now.  About a quart every other week.  New gaskets will seal it up about a month and the leak returns.  But it has never smelled like oil was starting to get hot or burn.  So I'd say your probably off the hook.  Sorry to hear about it though.  I am sure I would feel horrible if that happened to me too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||11-17-2000||06:46 PM||||Well, I just came from looking at it (and towing it to my storage yard) and I am certain it wasn't my fault.  Thank goodness!<P>The front half of the decklid is completely gone and a portion of the spoiler is melted.  It appears that the fire started on the drivers side of the engine, as that is where the majority of the damage is.<P>I still don't know what exactly started it, but it was just a coincidence that it happened after I changed the alternator.<P>I'll post some pictures as soon as I can....it just started snowing again, so it may  be a few days.||||reg||14
Z||000009||Black88GT||11-17-2000||08:49 PM||||You know those Fiero's, always catching on fire...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||10
