Z||000016||mrfiero||11-20-2000||01:10 PM||||Yes it is sad....it was a very well kept Fiero.  Plus it was relatively rare......it was one of 1201 '87 SE's that came with the 4-cyl.<P>I plan on buying it back from his insurance company as soon as everything gets settled, so yes.....I will be parting it out soon!<P>Those cars in the back ground are my parts cars/rebuilders.  There's a red '88 coupe, a burgundy '88 Formula, a black '84 econo coupe, a red '86 SE V-6 and a black '88 GT w/T-Tops.  <P>Right now just the '88 coupe and Formula are being parted out.  The '84 econo coupe just needs a slave cyl. to be driveable (only 91K miles on it), the '86 SE needs some engine work and the '88 GT needs a new engine altogether.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||wkayl||11-20-2000||01:39 PM||||Mike<BR>E-mail your address.  I may be coming through there sometime on Tuesday.<BR>Wayne<P>wkayl717@aol.com||||reg||1
Z||000018||theogre||11-20-2000||08:13 PM||||If you're pretty sure it started on the drivers side...... here's some posible causes.<P>automatic leaking ATF from a coolant line<BR>valve cover leaking down end of block<BR>electrical<P>there's not a bloody lot there to start a fire on that side.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||mrfiero||11-20-2000||09:38 PM||||It's a 5-sp., so no ATF leaks.  There was no evidence of oil leaking, so I tend to believe it was electrical.  Something shorted out and caught the vapor cannister on fire.  That's what I think, although I don't know what exactly shorted.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Daniel87GT||11-21-2000||12:17 PM||||I had an engine fire in my 85 2M4 that may have had a similar cause.  Basically, the positive battery lead goes right next to the exhaust.  So, over time, the insulation on the cable melted enough so that I got an arc between the battery cable & the exhaust.  I instantly had a fire when the wire's insulation lit up.  Fortuantely the car was in the middle of a safety & emissions, so it was noticed and put out before it caught anything else on fire.  All I had to do was replace the wire.||||reg||1
Z||000021||theogre||11-21-2000||08:32 PM||||One I left out..... they ran something over and caught it on the exhaust.<P>||||reg||1
